{
 "_comment": [
  "GENERATED ONCE from build.sh (2026-07-28), then hand-maintained.",
  "This is the build's SOURCE OF TRUTH for what userland exists and what",
  "gets staged onto the disk.  It was parsed out of build.sh rather than",
  "retyped, so the ninja graph started from exactly what build.sh built --",
  "131 byte-identical binaries and identical disk catalogs.",
  "Adding a tool: add an entry here, re-run tools/ninja/gen.py.",
  "disk_src/etc/rc is deliberately ABSENT: it is generated from rc.in by tools/make_ufsboot.sh. Staging it here made the image depend on a file its own build rewrites.",
  "jsh REMOVED 2026-07-29: bsh (2.11BSD Bourne) is /bin/sh and tcsh is the interactive shell, so jsh had no remaining role. Its /bin/sh FALLBACK is gone too -- vendor/ guarantees bsh builds, and that fallback is what silently staged the wrong shell on any tree without examples/."
 ],
